    "Description": "P1b (Hill-attack -> Blueprints migration), tree-INTEGRATION track (architect Q#9-A): the integrated twin of HillAssault2_CalculateSegments -- SAME SegmentMath.TotalSlots logic (GetParameter StartX/StartY/EndX/EndY/TankSpacing -> curated SegmentMath.TotalSlots pure FunctionCall), but leaves its native WorkingState EMPTY and converses over the standalone entity-scoped HillAttackSharedState struct via GetShared/SetShared(VariableId=\"state\"), so it can be composed alongside sibling integrated nodes in a real commander .btree.json without each node owning a colliding private WorkingState (per-blueprint WorkingState types never match byte-for-byte across distinct generated _Bp+WorkingState structs). Graph: EventEntry -> SetShared(\"state\") -> Return(Success), where SetShared.Value is fed by a chain of pure HillAttackSharedStateOps.With* FunctionCalls seeded from GetShared(\"state\").Value: WithTotalSlots(SegmentMath.TotalSlots(...)) -> WithBurnedSlotsMask((ushort)0) -> WithWaveUsedSlotsMask((ushort)0) -> WithBaselineReservedMask((ushort)0) -> WithCachedEqsRequestId(-1L) -> WithCachedTargetGroupHandle(-1) -> WithEqsRequestTime(0f) -> WithCurrentWave(0). Does not zero ActiveRunners -- mirrors the oracle/isolated-twin's CalculateSegments, which does not touch the runner tracker either. Does not modify the C# oracle, the isolated twin (HillAssault2_CalculateSegments.bp.json), or the compiler.",
